Regarding the a2[a/b/c/d] files, cmg stands for cell migration genes, and ngg stands for neurogenesis genes.

These genes have been extracted from the gene ontology analysis performed on some of the files in the "1_Intersections" folder.

I provided them here for to simplify the reproducibility. If you want to generate them on your own, the information is provided below.

The Gene Ontology analysis has been performed on lists of genes using Panther (https://geneontology.org).

Paste the desired list of genes in the box on the right where it says: 
GO Enrichment Analysis 
Powered by PANTHER

Make sure "biological process" is selected and "Mus musculus" is selected as the organism.

Click on "Launch".

After that, in a new browser tab, you will get the list of gene ontologies which provides you with information on what the genes you pasted are involved in.


